Maven's behavior when a dependency version is omitted in a sub-module's `pom.xml` is to first check its immediate parent's `<dependencyManagement>` section. If it's not found there, it then traverses up the hierarchy to the ultimate parent, which in this case is `spring-boot-starter-parent`.

I suspect that the previous "parent" POM (version `4.0.6`) we were using might have been more of a facade, implicitly providing certain dependencies. When I switched to a genuine `spring-boot-starter-parent` (version 3.2.5), this implicit behavior was altered, leading to the current dependency version resolution issues.

