properties from the root. And of course, I've nuked my local Maven cache with the `-U` flag and a good old `rm -rf`.

The fact that this standard artifact, `spring-boot-starter-webmvc`, is still proving elusive, whether it's the POM or the JAR, suggests something more fundamental is at play. I'm starting to suspect either I'm missing a crucial piece of the project's setup, or there's some bizarre quirk in the environment I'm working in. It's also possible, though I'm trying to rule this out, that my `spring-boot.version` property, even 
though it's correctly set to `3.2.5`, isn't resolving as expected when it tries to pull in `spring-boot-starter-webmvc`.

