The error message itself – `Could not find artifact org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-starter-webmvc:jar:3.2.5 in central (https://repo.maven.apache.org/maven2)` – is quite clear. It tells me that Maven is simply *unable to locate or download* this particular artifact, even though it's a fundamental and readily available Spring Boot dependency.

At this point, my strong conviction is that the issue lies *outside* of the `pom.xml` files themselves, assuming standard Maven behavior. I'm leaning towards a problem with my Maven environment's ability to resolve and download artifacts in general. This could manifest in several ways:

