Once I’ve cleaned up the root POM, my focus will shift to ensuring the inheritance structure is solid. I need to be absolutely certain that all my child modules are correctly inheriting from the parent POM. Beyond that, I'll be meticulously checking each child `pom.xml` for any conflicting definitions of the `spring-boot.version` property. It’s possible that an explicit override in a child module is interfering with the 
versioning defined in the parent BOM.

So, the immediate plan is to remove that explicit `spring-boot-starter-webmvc` dependency management entry from the root `pom.xml`. I'm going to rely on the `spring-boot-dependencies` import to manage it correctly.

