perhaps this explicit import is actually causing a conflict or is misconfigured 
in some way, and we should just rely on the `spring-boot-starter-parent` to do 
its job.

After all, the Spring Boot documentation is pretty clear on this: when you're 
using `spring-boot-starter-parent`, you typically don't need to manually import 
`spring-boot-dependencies` in your own `dependencyManagement`. The parent POM 
